# PQT Lab Control Center settings for the lab. It runs on central_server_pc,
# next to Central. Copy to C:\ProgramData\LabNet\control-center.env.
# Start by hand:  labnet-control-center --env-file C:\ProgramData\LabNet\control-center.env
#
# Start from the file `labnet-central-admin setup --user control-center
# --write-env ... --server-url http://127.0.0.1:8008` made: it already holds
# the two Central settings below. Development uses the same layout in
# .devnet/control-center.env (written by scripts/dev/seed.sh).

# Central on this same computer, over loopback: no CA file needed.
LABNET_SERVER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8008
LABNET_API_KEY=<from setup --write-env>

# The built-in server is plain HTTP on loopback. Caddy serves it to the lab
# over HTTPS (see Labnet/README.md, "Control Center").
LABNET_CONTROL_CENTER_HOST=127.0.0.1
LABNET_CONTROL_CENTER_PORT=8080

# Logins: each person signs in to Caddy with their own login, and Caddy adds
# this secret to every request. With it set, only requests through Caddy get
# in. Don't write it by hand: scripts/lab/setup_logins.ps1 sets this line and
# writes the matching Caddy snippet (see Labnet/README.md, "Logins").
# At least 32 printable ASCII characters, no spaces. Unset: no logins
# (development on one computer only).
# LABNET_CONTROL_CENTER_PROXY_SECRET=<written by setup_logins.ps1>

# Host names the pages answer to, comma-separated, no ports or schemes.
# Default: 127.0.0.1,localhost without the secret above; any host with it.
# Without logins, Caddy's name must be listed or every page answers 400.
# LABNET_CONTROL_CENTER_ALLOWED_HOSTS=pqt-control-center,192.168.50.10

# How often the network picture is refreshed from Central (seconds).
# LABNET_CONTROL_CENTER_REFRESH_SECONDS=3

# Device control pages (defaults shown): Play stops itself after
# MAX_HOLD_MINUTES, a page releases its device IDLE_RELEASE_SECONDS after the
# last viewer leaves, and a script is stopped after SCRIPT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS.
# LABNET_CONTROL_CENTER_MAX_HOLD_MINUTES=30
# LABNET_CONTROL_CENTER_IDLE_RELEASE_SECONDS=15
# LABNET_CONTROL_CENTER_SCRIPT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=600

# The Experiments tab saves one JSON file per experiment here. Default:
# .\experiments next to this file. Back it up with the rest of LabNet's data.
# LABNET_CONTROL_CENTER_EXPERIMENTS_DIR=C:\ProgramData\LabNet\experiments

# The Automation tab keeps its projects here: projects\ (people's and agents'
# files) and state\ (the Control Center's own). Default: .\automation next to
# this file. Back it up too. Uploads are limited to MAX_FILE_MB per file,
# and everything one run's runner uploads to RUN_QUOTA_MB in all. An active
# run whose runner says nothing for RUN_STALE_MINUTES is marked failed.
# Runner tokens: labnet-control-center-admin --env-file <this file> runner add NAME
# LABNET_AUTOMATION_DIR=C:\ProgramData\LabNet\automation
# LABNET_AUTOMATION_MAX_FILE_MB=100
# LABNET_AUTOMATION_RUN_QUOTA_MB=500
# LABNET_AUTOMATION_RUN_STALE_MINUTES=10
# An approved protocol holds its devices at most GRANT_MAX_MINUTES (1 to 1440;
# a protocol asking for longer is refused). A protocol nobody approves or
# rejects within APPROVAL_HOURS fails its run.
# LABNET_AUTOMATION_GRANT_MAX_MINUTES=120
# LABNET_AUTOMATION_APPROVAL_HOURS=24

# Photo-Agent (the chat sidebar) runs Claude Code (`claude -p`) with the login
# of the Windows account that starts the Control Center: as that account,
# install Claude Code, run `claude` once and /login. No API key is used.
# It may read only these folders (';'-separated); default: the installed
# labnet package. Its workspace defaults to .\agent next to this file.
# LABNET_AGENT_SOURCES=C:\ProgramData\LabNet\control-center-venv\Lib\site-packages\labnet;C:\ProgramData\LabNet\client-examples
# The lab library: papers in topic folders, plus collections\<name>.txt
# reading lists. Photo-Agent and every Automation project read it.
# LABNET_AGENT_LITERATURE_DIR=C:\ProgramData\LabNet\literature
# The chat's model menu (aliases or full model ids), the model and effort
# selected at first. Each viewer can change both per message.
# LABNET_AGENT_MODELS=fable,opus,sonnet,haiku
# LABNET_AGENT_MODEL=sonnet
# LABNET_AGENT_EFFORT=high
# LABNET_AGENT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=300
# LABNET_AGENT_MAX_CONCURRENT=2
# LABNET_AGENT_COMMAND=C:\Users\<account>\.local\bin\claude.exe
